Use the front-view and side-view photographs together.
Before estimating any measurement, validate both photographs independently. A valid pair must
meet every condition below:
- exactly one person is visible in each photograph;
- the entire head, recognizable face, and both feet are visible in each photograph;
- the body is not cropped and is visible from the top of the head through both feet;
- the first photograph is a true front view and the second is a true side view;
- both photographs are sufficiently bright and sharp to inspect the body outline.

Set photo_valid to false when any condition fails. Select the single most useful primary
failure_reason from the schema enum. Do not infer a missing body region from height, weight,
gender, or population averages. When photo_valid is false, return null for every measurement.
Set photo_valid to true and failure_reason to "none" only when every validation flag is true.

